          "cap": "Benozzo Gozzoli, The Triumph of Saint Thomas Aquinas (c. 1470–75; Louvre). Aquinas sits enthroned with Aristotle and Plato flanking him and Averroes lying prostrate beneath — the painting diagrams his influences as a theological program. A 15th-century imagining, painted to celebrate the Thomist synthesis; the prostrate Averroes is a Christian-triumphalist statement about which authority won, not a record of any real encounter.",
